"{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"thread\":{\"id\":\"01a044b8-39b5-7240-8406-c08a614deaa8\",\"kind\":\"codex\",\"hostId\":\"remote-ssh-discovered:black-chatgpt-2\",\"title\":\"Operator MFP L=2, general t (2)\",\"preview\":\"can you read about MFP (mean field peeling) from this project?&#x20;\",\"status\":{\"type\":\"notLoaded\"},\"cwd\":\"/home/amir/Codes/PDE\",\"createdAt\":1787859319,\"updatedAt\":1787859319},\"page\":{\"order\":\"newest_first\",\"limit\":10,\"nextCursor\":\"01a03a63-b192-7db2-baf3-426da385d235\",\"hasMore\":true},\"turns\":[{\"id\":\"01a06e36-7975-7500-88f3-1be2a7180e67\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"error\":null,\"startedAt\":1788555458,\"completedAt\":1788556030,\"durationMs\":571804,\"items\":[{\"type\":\"contextCompaction\",\"id\":\"item-1781\"},{\"type\":\"userMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1782\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"can you output the fully self contained complete and rigorous and rigorous proof of the L=3 statement that you just proved? include the proof in sufficient detail that it can be read and verified and checked in full. run some audits on the report, with the sub agnnts auditing only receiving the self contained report and nothing else , to avoid biases, and see if all audits pass, if some issues arise, fix them and redo the independent self contained isolated agents. do these rounds until the agent passes all are clean\"}]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1783\",\"text\":\"The audits found a substantive gap in the proposed \\\\(L=3\\\\) proof: the estimates supplied do not justify the joint width/time limit. I’m checking the corrected self-contained report and the final isolated audits so I can give you a precise account of what is proved and what remains unresolved.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1784\",\"summary\":[\"**Rechecking detailed proof**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_oS1DtMpPAijQyf3iHJfGmr8C\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-1b2c-75a1-bd2f-06abe96a49d3\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_math_audit\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_HSJtSt8EDKnvsxPI8LulPl4T\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-3683-7702-9a24-9d2742546151\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_limit_audit\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1785\",\"summary\":[\"**Checking theorem response currents**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_iJ3ZcwrhO8OpQ63qcycXtFDA\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-1b2c-75a1-bd2f-06abe96a49d3\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_math_audit\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1786\",\"summary\":[\"**Checking Gaussian tail bounds**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1787\",\"text\":\"A concrete check now isolates the failure without assuming that a continuous-time limit exists. After one exact Euler step, a backpropagated field has a nondegenerate Gaussian width limit, so its \\\\(L^q\\\\) norm grows as \\\\(\\\\sqrt q\\\\). The proposed stability bound omitted that growth. I’m incorporating this check into the report and having the isolated auditors verify it.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"fileChange\",\"id\":\"exec-0e67d466-8327-4584-a779-2d1e5d2c1d7b\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/tmp/l3_joint_limit_audited_report.md\",\"kind\":{\"type\":\"update\",\"move_path\":null},\"diff\":{\"text\":\"@@ -286,4 +286,5 @@\\n \\n-The discarded draft claimed, with one constant \\\\(K\\\\) independent of \\\\(q,T\\\\),\\n-uniformly for every \\\\(q\\\\ge2\\\\) and small \\\\(T\\\\),\\n+The discarded draft needed the following estimate with one constant \\\\(K\\\\)\\n+independent of \\\\(q,T\\\\), uniformly for every \\\\(q\\\\ge2\\\\), small \\\\(T\\\\), and\\n+the discrete meshes used to construct the flow:\\n \\n@@ -293,29 +294,45 @@\\n \\n-Even its prefactor is false.  Take \\\\(p=d=1\\\\), \\\\(x=y=1\\\\).  In the limiting\\n-initialization, \\\\(C(0)=0,e(0)=-1,\\\\gamma=2\\\\), and therefore\\n+This mesh-uniform estimate is false.  Take \\\\(p=d=1\\\\), \\\\(x=y=1\\\\), and\\n+consider exactly one Euler step of size \\\\(h>0\\\\).  First set \\\\(C_0=0\\\\)\\n+at finite width.  Then \\\\(e_0=-1,\\\\gamma=2\\\\); every hidden update vanishes\\n+in that step, while\\n \\n \\\\[\\n- \\\\dot C(0)=2H_3,\\\\qquad\\n- \\\\dot D_3(0)=2H_3\\\\phi'(S_3)=2\\\\cos(2S_3).                  \\\\tag{4.4}\\n+ C_1=2hH_{3,0},\\\\qquad\\n+ D_{3,1}=2hH_{3,0}\\\\phi'(S_{3,0})\\n+         =2h\\\\cos(2S_{3,0}).                              \\\\tag{4.4}\\n \\\\]\\n \\n-Since \\\\(B_3(t)=A_3+O(t^2)\\\\),\\n+Consequently, with \\\\(A_3=B_{3,0}\\\\), the identity\\n \\n \\\\[\\n- \\\\dot P_2(0)=A_3^T(2\\\\cos(2S_3)).                          \\\\tag{4.5}\\n+ P_{2,1}(h)=2hA_3^T\\\\cos(2S_{3,0})                        \\\\tag{4.5}\\n \\\\]\\n \\n-Formula (3.2) shows that (4.5) contains an independent centered Gaussian\\n-innovation of variance\\n+is exact.  In the fixed-program width limit, \\\\(S_{3,0}\\\\) has the standard\\n+normal law: all preceding activation second moments are one.\\n+For \\\\(Z\\\\sim N(0,1)\\\\), the reused-adjoint response in (3.2) is\\n+\\\\(\\\\mathbb E[-2\\\\sin(2Z)]=0\\\\).  Therefore the limit of (4.5) is exactly\\n+\\\\(h\\\\sigma\\\\Gamma\\\\), where \\\\(\\\\Gamma\\\\sim N(0,1)\\\\) and\\n \\n \\\\[\\n- 4\\\\mathbb E\\\\cos^2(2S_3)>0.                                \\\\tag{4.6}\\n+ \\\\sigma^2=4\\\\mathbb E\\\\cos^2(2Z)=2(1+e^{-8})>0.             \\\\tag{4.6}\\n \\\\]\\n \\n-Hence \\\\(\\\\|\\\\dot P_2(0)\\\\|_q\\\\asymp\\\\sqrt q\\\\).  For each fixed \\\\(q\\\\), smoothness\\n-of the finite-step Gaussian DAG gives \\\\(P_2(t)/t\\\\to\\\\dot P_2(0)\\\\) in \\\\(L^q\\\\)\\n-(all activation derivatives are bounded and every zero-time Gaussian\\n-moment is finite).  If (4.3) held for every \\\\(T=t\\\\), division by \\\\(t\\\\)\\n-followed by \\\\(t\\\\downarrow0\\\\) would therefore give a bound independent of\\n-\\\\(q\\\\), contradicting (4.6).\\n+The actual initialization \\\\(C_0=n^{-1}Z_C\\\\) gives the same one-step limit\\n+by Theorem G.4: its initial scalar \\\\(n^{-1}\\\\) converges to zero, and the\\n+recursive limiting program is the one just computed.  The theorem also\\n+passes every fixed \\\\(q\\\\)-th absolute moment.  If (4.3) held for these\\n+one-step limits with \\\\(T=h\\\\), it would imply\\n+\\\\(\\\\sigma\\\\|\\\\Gamma\\\\|_q\\\\le K e^{Khq}\\\\).  First send \\\\(h\\\\downarrow0\\\\) at a\\n+fixed \\\\(q\\\\), then let \\\\(q\\\\to\\\\infty\\\\).  This contradicts\\n+\\\\[\\n+ \\\\|\\\\Gamma\\\\|_q=\\n+ \\\\left(\\\\frac{2^{q/2}\\\\Gamma((q+1)/2)}{\\\\sqrt\\\\pi}\\\\right)^{1/q}\\n+ \\\\longrightarrow\\\\infty.\\n+\\\\]\\n+This countercheck uses only one fixed finite program.  It assumes neither\\n+existence nor differentiability of a continuous width-first flow.  It\\n+refutes the mesh-uniform bound needed by the discarded construction; it\\n+does not by itself rule out a differently stated continuous-only estimate.\\n \\n@@ -782,8 +799,11 @@\\n \\n-Equivalently, an all-source proof should assign weight one to each \\\\(P_2\\\\)\\n-mark and weight two to each \\\\(P_1\\\\) mark, and prove that a connected\\n-finite-width causal component with \\\\(q\\\\) strict time edges has total weight\\n-at most \\\\(2q+O(1)\\\\).  Crucially, this must include all higher Malliavin\\n-orders, derivatives of empirical moment scalars, and a controlled remainder,\\n-not just the first-source limiting response spine.\\n+A possible combinatorial approach is to assign weight one to each \\\\(P_2\\\\)\\n+mark and weight two to each \\\\(P_1\\\\) mark, and seek a bound on the total\\n+weight of each connected finite-width causal component in terms of its\\n+number of strict time edges.  Such a bound would still have to be proved\\n+and converted into (6.11), including summation over components and a\\n+controlled remainder.  In particular, it would need to include all higher\\n+Malliavin orders and derivatives of empirical moment scalars, rather than\\n+only the first-source limiting response spine.  No equivalence between\\n+such a combinatorial statement and (6.11) is asserted here.\\n \\n\",\"truncated\":false}}]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_brtqwnOBMRW4tHFx0eoETFlZ\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-1b2c-75a1-bd2f-06abe96a49d3\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_math_audit\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_7OZbZsc0TN0dJy2dGMjZ5YG1\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-3683-7702-9a24-9d2742546151\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_limit_audit\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1788\",\"summary\":[\"**Restricting fixed-R closure**\",\"**Refining the restricted closure**\",\"**Restricting fixed-R closure**\",\"**Refining the restricted closure**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"fileChange\",\"id\":\"exec-f872cc5a-6526-4919-bee2-846329680508\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/tmp/l3_joint_limit_audited_report.md\",\"kind\":{\"type\":\"update\",\"move_path\":null},\"diff\":{\"text\":\"@@ -697,8 +697,11 @@\\n Estimate (6.7) gives a width-independent finite-dimensional Euler estimate\\n-\\\\(C_{R,T}|\\\\pi|\\\\) in \\\\(\\\\rho_n\\\\).  A candidate action topology can then be specified as\\n-follows.  Enumerate all finite typed probes generated from the current core\\n-vectors by \\\\(B_2,B_2^T,B_3,B_3^T\\\\), the maps\\n-\\\\(\\\\phi,\\\\phi',\\\\chi_R\\\\), rational linear combinations, the coordinatewise\\n-products occurring in the exact DAG (each has a uniformly bounded factor),\\n-and normalized inner products.  If \\\\(\\\\mathcal L_n(P_m)\\\\) is the empirical coordinate law of the\\n+\\\\(C_{R,T}|\\\\pi|\\\\) in \\\\(\\\\rho_n\\\\).  A restricted candidate action topology can\\n+then be specified as follows.  Enumerate the finite typed probes generated\\n+from the current core vectors by \\\\(B_2,B_2^T,B_3,B_3^T\\\\), the maps\\n+\\\\(\\\\phi,\\\\phi',\\\\chi_R\\\\), rational linear combinations, normalized inner\\n+products, and coordinatewise products only when both factors have a proved\\n+uniform \\\\(L^\\\\infty\\\\) bound on (6.1).  The \\\\(C\\\\) coordinate is such a bounded\\n+factor; \\\\(U\\\\) and arbitrary matrix images need not be.  This restriction\\n+includes all products in the independent-coordinate cutoff update itself.\\n+If \\\\(\\\\mathcal L_n(P_m)\\\\) is the empirical coordinate law of the\\n tuple returned by probe \\\\(P_m\\\\), set\\n@@ -716,5 +719,17 @@\\n (6.7), followed by (6.4), supplies the width-uniform comparison between\\n-meshes for each fixed physical probe.  What is not written out here is the\\n-completion, realization, and restartability of the resulting entire probe\\n-algebra.\\n+meshes for each probe in this restricted algebra.  This follows by\\n+induction on its finite construction: operator multiplication uses\\n+\\\\(\\\\|Bu-\\\\widetilde B\\\\widetilde u\\\\|_2\\\\le\\n+\\\\|B-\\\\widetilde B\\\\|_{\\\\rm op}\\\\|u\\\\|_2+\\n+\\\\|\\\\widetilde B\\\\|_{\\\\rm op}\\\\|u-\\\\widetilde u\\\\|_2\\\\);\\n+coordinate maps use their Lipschitz constants; inner products use\\n+Cauchy--Schwarz; and products use the two \\\\(L^\\\\infty\\\\) bounds.  One\\n+bounded but varying factor would not suffice for the last step, because\\n+\\\\(\\\\widetilde u(b-\\\\widetilde b)\\\\) need not be controlled in \\\\(L^2\\\\)\\n+when \\\\(\\\\widetilde u\\\\) is unbounded.  Extension to larger probe algebras,\\n+including all uncut physical velocity expressions, requires additional\\n+uniform integrability and continuity arguments.\\n+\\n+What is not written out here is the completion, realization, and\\n+restartability even of the restricted limiting probe algebra.\\n \\n@@ -796,4 +811,10 @@\\n \\n-Together with a fully constructed fixed-cutoff limit, (6.14) makes those limiting\\n-trajectories Cauchy as \\\\(R\\\\to\\\\infty\\\\) and identifies the uncut joint limit.\\n+Estimate (6.14) would compare the core finite-width trajectories with their\\n+cutoff versions.  To convert it into the requested full joint theorem,\\n+one must additionally construct the fixed-cutoff law-level limits,\\n+transfer this comparison to an \\\\(R\\\\)-independent closing topology, pass\\n+all uncut velocity and kernel expressions using sufficient uniform\\n+integrability, and prove well-posedness and restartability in that\\n+topology.  These conclusions are not asserted to follow from (6.14)\\n+alone, and those remaining arguments are not supplied here.\\n \\n\",\"truncated\":false}}]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_baAEmOlNhnIH3eqzCDN8dVQv\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-1b2c-75a1-bd2f-06abe96a49d3\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_math_audit\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_mxzEluy3shhRrO1vnavhgahG\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-3683-7702-9a24-9d2742546151\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_limit_audit\"},{\"type\":\"webSearch\",\"id\":\"exec-7cf74476-f2a2-4669-b639-8d3b5ba746bf\",\"query\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/yang21c/yang21c-supp.pdf\",\"action\":{\"type\":\"openPage\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/yang21c/yang21c-supp.pdf\"}},{\"type\":\"webSearch\",\"id\":\"exec-c45d92e2-d13c-4242-a2a7-2ff548f3e934\",\"query\":\"'Theorem G.4'\",\"action\":{\"type\":\"findInPage\",\"url\":null,\"pattern\":\"Theorem G.4\"}},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"subagent-completed-01a06e38-36c5-7300-aba4-eec9e893b9ed\",\"kind\":\"completed\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-3683-7702-9a24-9d2742546151\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_limit_audit\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"subagent-completed-01a06e38-1b69-7a50-9166-244c7d9aed74\",\"kind\":\"completed\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e38-1b2c-75a1-bd2f-06abe96a49d3\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/report_only_math_audit\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1789\",\"summary\":[\"**Adding explicit U-bound report**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"fileChange\",\"id\":\"exec-025e4824-8fc5-4593-a1db-663ccefce454\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/tmp/l3_joint_limit_audited_report.md\",\"kind\":{\"type\":\"update\",\"move_path\":null},\"diff\":{\"text\":\"@@ -569,3 +569,4 @@\\n \\n-Choose an odd \\\\(C^\\\\infty\\\\), 1-Lipschitz map \\\\(\\\\chi_R\\\\) which equals the\\n+For each integer \\\\(R\\\\ge1\\\\), choose an odd \\\\(C^\\\\infty\\\\), 1-Lipschitz map\\n+\\\\(\\\\chi_R\\\\) which equals the\\n identity on \\\\([-R,R]\\\\), is constant outside \\\\([-R-2,R+2]\\\\), and satisfies\\n@@ -681,4 +682,14 @@\\n \\\\(|\\\\chi_R(P_2)|\\\\le|P_2|\\\\) bounds \\\\(\\\\|D_2\\\\|_2\\\\), and (2.7) finally bounds\\n-\\\\(\\\\|B_2-A_2\\\\|_{\\\\rm op}\\\\).  The forward \\\\(Z_\\\\ell\\\\)'s are bounded in \\\\(L^2\\\\)\\n-by the operator bounds and \\\\(|H_\\\\ell|\\\\le\\\\sqrt2\\\\).\\n+\\\\(\\\\|B_2-A_2\\\\|_{\\\\rm op}\\\\).  The deeper preactivations \\\\(S_2,S_3\\\\) are\\n+bounded in \\\\(L^2\\\\) by the operator bounds and \\\\(|H_\\\\ell|\\\\le\\\\sqrt2\\\\).\\n+For the first layer, (2.8), \\\\(|G_{ab}|\\\\le1\\\\), and\\n+\\\\(\\\\|\\\\chi_R(P_1^b)\\\\|_{2,n}\\\\le\\\\|P_1^b\\\\|_{2,n}\\n+\\\\le\\\\|B_2\\\\|_{\\\\rm op}\\\\|D_2^b\\\\|_{2,n}\\\\) give\\n+\\\\[\\n+ \\\\|\\\\dot U^a\\\\|_{2,n}\\n+ \\\\le\\\\gamma\\\\sqrt2\\\\sum_b |e_b|\\\\,\\n+          \\\\|B_2\\\\|_{\\\\rm op}\\\\|D_2^b\\\\|_{2,n}.\\n+\\\\]\\n+Integration bounds \\\\(\\\\|U^a(t)\\\\|_{2,n}\\\\) from its initial value, with no\\n+dependence on \\\\(R\\\\).\\n \\n@@ -694,3 +705,5 @@\\n Also \\\\(\\\\|C(0)\\\\|_\\\\infty=n^{-1}\\\\max_i|Z_i|\\\\to0\\\\) in\\n-probability by a Gaussian union bound.\\n+probability by a Gaussian union bound, and\\n+\\\\(\\\\max_a\\\\|U^a(0)\\\\|_{2,n}^2\\\\to1\\\\) in probability by the law of large\\n+numbers for the fixed finite family of standard-Gaussian marginals.\\n \\n@@ -748,3 +761,3 @@\\n    \\\\exp\\\\!\\\\left({|P_{2,i}^a(t)|^2\\\\over K^2T^2}\\\\right),\\\\\\\\\\n- Z_{1,n}&=\\\\sup_{t\\\\le T,a,\\\\ R\\\\in\\\\mathbb N}{1\\\\over n}\\\\sum_i\\n+ Z_{1,n}&=\\\\sup_{t\\\\le T,a,\\\\ R\\\\in\\\\mathbb N_{\\\\ge1}}{1\\\\over n}\\\\sum_i\\n    \\\\exp\\\\!\\\\left({|P_{1,i}^a(t)|\\\\vee|P_{1,R,i}^a(t)|\\\\over KT}\\\\right).\\n\",\"truncated\":false}}]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1790\",\"text\":\"Both reviewers accepted the corrected report within its stated scope. The full \\\\(L=3\\\\) theorem still lacks a uniform tail/stability estimate and the construction of a closing, restartable law-level state. I’m sending the final report to fresh reviewers with no earlier discussion, as you requested.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_FkCiZjlGchAEBHgmtIKzKcDd\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e3b-b7ac-7002-9e94-147cadb09b24\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/final_report_blind_a\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_BSe7IguFfYUSb9S7AZJIhWPR\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e3b-d0a2-7e50-b07e-ed3b6b4fc510\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/final_report_blind_b\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1791\",\"summary\":[\"**Preparing audit report**\",\"**Exploring activation transforms**\",\"**Preparing audit report**\",\"**Exploring activation transforms**\",\"**Assessing ODE uniqueness**\",\"**Preparing audit report**\",\"**Exploring activation transforms**\",\"**Assessing ODE uniqueness**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"webSearch\",\"id\":\"exec-38457522-d97d-4f8d-81b1-8ffaf47fa67f\",\"query\":\"\",\"action\":{\"type\":\"other\"}},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1792\",\"summary\":[\"**Checking q-moment formula**\",\"**Checking hidden-layer acceleration**\",\"**Checking q-moment formula**\",\"**Checking hidden-layer acceleration**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1793\",\"text\":\"The source checks confirm that the Tensor Program theorem covers the reused-matrix dependencies and singular Gaussian covariances for each fixed finite computation. It does not provide the estimates needed as the number of GD steps diverges. The remaining issue is the passage to continuous time, beyond what the cited theorem asserts.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"subagent-completed-01a06e3b-d0e8-71b2-940e-89e80e22098e\",\"kind\":\"completed\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e3b-d0a2-7e50-b07e-ed3b6b4fc510\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/final_report_blind_b\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1794\",\"summary\":[\"**Retracting the theorem claim**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_VYvGMR8779csBrhNpGvSfuQ3\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e3b-b7ac-7002-9e94-147cadb09b24\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/final_report_blind_a\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1795\",\"summary\":[\"**Cleaning the current file**\",\"**Checking the tail-time condition**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"subagent-completed-01a06e3b-b7e9-78b2-bec2-2272aa535819\",\"kind\":\"completed\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a06e3b-b7ac-7002-9e94-147cadb09b24\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/final_report_blind_a\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1796\",\"summary\":[\"**Cleaning the current file**\",\"**Checking the tail-time condition**\",\"**Verifying the norm contradiction**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1797\",\"text\":\"I must retract the claim that the full \\\\(L=3\\\\) theorem was proved. The isolated audits exposed a substantive gap; I cannot present the argument as a complete proof.\\n\\nThe [corrected self-contained report](/tmp/l3_joint_limit_audited_report.md) contains the exact finite-width equations, verified fixed-step Gaussian recursion, explicit Gaussian calculations, and the precise failures of the proposed continuous-time argument.\\n\\nOne decisive error admits a direct check. For the proposed activation\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\phi(z)=\\\\sin z+\\\\cos z,\\n\\\\]\\nthe one-step width limit of the backpropagated field is\\n\\\\[\\nP_{2,1}(h)\\\\ \\\\overset{d}{=}\\\\ h\\\\sigma\\\\Gamma,\\n\\\\qquad\\n\\\\sigma^2=2(1+e^{-8}),\\\\qquad \\\\Gamma\\\\sim N(0,1).\\n\\\\]\\nThis follows from the exact one-step update\\n\\\\[\\nP_{2,1}(h)=2hA_3^\\\\top\\\\cos(2S_{3,0}),\\n\\\\]\\nwhose Gaussian response coefficient vanishes by symmetry.\\n\\nConsequently, the proposed estimate\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\|P_{2,1}(h)\\\\|_q\\\\le Kh\\\\,e^{Khq}\\n\\\\]\\ncannot hold with \\\\(K\\\\) independent of \\\\(q\\\\) and small \\\\(h\\\\). Dividing by \\\\(h\\\\) and sending \\\\(h\\\\downarrow0\\\\), at fixed \\\\(q\\\\), would give\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\sigma\\\\|\\\\Gamma\\\\|_q\\\\le K,\\n\\\\]\\nwhereas Gaussian \\\\(L^q\\\\) norms diverge as \\\\(q\\\\to\\\\infty\\\\). This check uses a fixed-step width limit and assumes no continuous limiting trajectory.\\n\\nThe external theorem was also checked against its full primary text. It establishes convergence for fixed finite tensor programs; it does not supply the uniform estimates needed for a diverging number of GD steps. [Yang–Hu, supplement, Theorem G.4 and Appendix A](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/yang21c/yang21c-supp.pdf)\\n\\nThe remaining gaps are uniform control of the uncut backpropagated fields and construction of the closing autonomous law-level evolution, including passage of all required products and path observables.\\n\\nFour isolated reviewers audited the report across two rounds. After corrections, both fresh final reviewers returned **PASS for the corrected report’s stated scope**. They explicitly did **not** certify the requested joint-limit theorem.\\n\\nThus the report documents a failed proof and verified partial results. The unconditional \\\\(L=3\\\\) theorem remains unresolved by this work.\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}]},{\"id\":\"01a044d0-e8bd-7b63-ae2b-b1357255c242\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"error\":null,\"startedAt\":1787860936,\"completedAt\":1787863060,\"durationMs\":2123383,\"items\":[{\"type\":\"userMessage\",\"id\":\"i