een reduced to a cleaner statement than the earlier continuous-response approach:\\n\\n- use the external Gaussian-program theorem only at a fixed auxiliary mesh;\\n- prove width-uniform Euler stability for a clipped current-operator ODE;\\n- obtain a cutoff-uniform sub-Gaussian bound from the exact causal response recursion;\\n- remove the cutoff by comparing the exact uncut finite-width ODE directly to the cutoff ODE.\\n\\nThe key comparison uses only the cutoff field:\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\phi'(U)P-\\\\phi'(U_R)\\\\tau_R(P_R)\\n=\\n\\\\phi'(U)(P-P_R)\\n+\\\\phi'(U)(P_R-\\\\tau_R(P_R))\\n+\\\\bigl(\\\\phi'(U)-\\\\phi'(U_R)\\\\bigr)\\\\tau_R(P_R).\\n\\\\]\\nSo no unproved tail bound for the uncut finite-width dynamics is being smuggled in. Two agents are now auditing precisely the uniform response-tail lemma and this cutoff-removal step.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1387\",\"summary\":[\"**Analyzing singular covariance in lemma**\",\"**Analyzing singular covariance in lemma**\",\"**Formulating formal response proposition**\",\"**Analyzing singular covariance in lemma**\",\"**Formulating formal response proposition**\",\"**Establishing subgaussian tail bounds in continuous limit**\",\"**Analyzing singular covariance in lemma**\",\"**Formulating formal response proposition**\",\"**Establishing subgaussian tail bounds in continuous limit**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"webSearch\",\"id\":\"exec-1cdc4f0a-75ec-4b3d-bb6b-094d0c6540d5\",\"query\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.19061\",\"action\":{\"type\":\"openPage\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.19061\"}},{\"type\":\"webSearch\",\"id\":\"exec-c3a65a1a-2df3-44ae-94b7-f4ba8518235b\",\"query\":\"arXiv 2406.19061 Qiyang Han Entrywise dynamics universality general first order methods\",\"action\":{\"type\":\"search\",\"query\":\"arXiv 2406.19061 Qiyang Han Entrywise dynamics universality general first order methods\",\"queries\":null}},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1388\",\"summary\